<title>UK: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>UNITED KINGDOM GOVERNMENT LIST (970502-2)</p>
<p>**************************************************************</p>
<p>* 1 May 97 - The Labour Party under Tony Blair were returned *</p>
<p>*		to power for the first time since 1979, heavily *</p>
<p>*		defeating John Major's Conservatives.	     *</p>
<p>**************************************************************</p>
<p> Head of State...............Queen ELIZABETH II</p>
<p>				- - - - - - - -</p>
<p>LABOUR PARTY GOVERNMENT (Formed 2 May 97)</p>
<p> Prime Minister.......Tony BLAIR</p>
<p>(Also First Lord of the Treasury &amp; Minister for</p>
<p>the Civil Service)</p>
<p> Deputy Prime Minister............John PRESCOTT</p>
<p>(With extra responsibilities for Environment, Transport</p>
<p>and regional policy)</p>
<p> Lord Chancellor...........Lord IRVINE of Lairg</p>
<p>				- - - - - - - -</p>
<p>CABINET (announced so far)</p>
<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer</p>
<p>    (Finance Minister).............Gordon BROWN</p>
<p> Education Secretary.............David BLUNKETT</p>
<p> Foreign &amp; Commonwealth Affairs Secretary...........Robin COOK</p>
<p>Home Secretary (Interior Minister)..Jack STRAW</p>
<p>President of the Board of Trade</p>
<p>    (Trade Secretary)..........Margaret BECKETT</p>
<p>				- - - - - - - -</p>
<p>Speaker of the House of Commons</p>
<p>    (lower house)...............Betty BOOTHROYD</p>
<p>				- - - - - - - -</p>
<p> Bank of England (Central Bank) Governor..........Eddie GEORGE</p>
<p>				- - - - - - - -</p>
<p>	 NOTE: Any comments/queries on the content of this</p>
<p>		 government list, please contact the Reuter</p>
<p>		 Editorial Reference Unit, London, on (171) 542</p>
<p>		 7968.</p>
<p>			   (End Government List)</p>
</text>
